From: Daniel Casota <dcasota@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 04:34:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] phc2sys: exit cleanly when stopped while waiting for ptp4l

phc2sys.service (OPTIONS="-a -r") waits for ptp4l before it does anything
("Waiting for ptp4l..."). Stopping it in that state always failed: SIGTERM
interrupts poll() in pmc_agent's run_pmc(), which logs "poll failed" at
error priority and returns RUN_PMC_INTR, auto_init_ports() treats the
-EINTR as fatal, and phc2sys exits with status 255, so systemd records the
unit as failed (Result=exit-code). The same applies to the -w wait in the
non-automatic mode.

pmc_agent.c: a poll() interrupted by a signal (SIGTERM on stop) is not a
failure, so do not log "poll failed" for EINTR.

phc2sys.c: an -EINTR while waiting for ptp4l returns only when the stop was
requested (is_running() is false), and main() then exits with 0: stopped
while waiting for ptp4l is a clean exit. Any other error, or an interrupt
while still running, ends as before.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Casota <dcasota@gmail.com>
---
 phc2sys.c   | 12 +++++++++---
 pmc_agent.c |  3 ++-
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/phc2sys.c b/phc2sys.c
--- a/phc2sys.c
+++ b/phc2sys.c
@@ -944,7 +944,7 @@ static int auto_init_ports(struct domain *domain)
 		}
 		if (err == -ETIMEDOUT) {
 			pr_notice("Waiting for ptp4l...");
-		} else {
+		} else if (err != -EINTR || is_running()) {
 			return -1;
 		}
 	}
@@ -1480,8 +1480,11 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])
 			if (init_pmc_node(cfg, domains[i].agent, uds_local,
 					  phc2sys_recv_subscribed, &domains[i]))
 				goto end;
-			if (auto_init_ports(&domains[i]) < 0)
+			if (auto_init_ports(&domains[i]) < 0) {
+				if (!is_running())
+					r = 0;
 				goto end;
+			}
 		}
 		r = do_loop(domains, n_domains);
 		goto end;
@@ -1518,8 +1521,11 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])
 
 		while (is_running()) {
 			r = run_pmc_wait_sync(domains[0].agent, 1000);
-			if (r < 0)
+			if (r < 0) {
+				if (!is_running())
+					r = 0;
 				goto end;
+			}
 			if (r > 0)
 				break;
 			else
diff --git a/pmc_agent.c b/pmc_agent.c
--- a/pmc_agent.c
+++ b/pmc_agent.c
@@ -136,7 +136,8 @@ static int run_pmc(struct pmc_agent *node, int timeout, int ds_id,
 
 		cnt = poll(pollfd, N_FD, timeout);
 		if (cnt < 0) {
-			pr_err("poll failed");
+			if (errno != EINTR)
+				pr_err("poll failed");
 			return RUN_PMC_INTR;
 		}
 		if (!cnt) {
-- 
2.53.0

